f pieces because  many of the pieces in the demo build and  the lifestream build during Gamescom had  very yeah few ree colorable options and  but yeah i think that's just something  related to the british and generic theme  that was in that in that build of the  game because the building sets in this  map show a lot of recolor ball building  pieces and I have to say recolor ability  is a bit of a trade off as well  recoverable items always have no  slightly less nuances slightly less  detail  on the textures then non-recoverable  items so I think for brick was things  like that it's quite all right  to have no recoverable options although  I suppose the best situation would be to  have a non recoverable wall and then a  another recolor ball kind of similar  piece with just a different texture that  recolor is better the only thing that  I'm a bit concerned about here is I do  hope that those brown pieces are  recoverable as well but aside from that  the whole set looks entirely recoverable  so that's good anyway those were all my  thoughts about planets ooh based on  Gamescom I know there's a lot of things  that I didn't really touch upon like the  electricity or water management's or  certain elements of managing animals and  stuff but these are really just general  things that I thought have been much  more talked about in other live streams  other YouTube content and by frontier  themselves this video is just some of  the things that stuck out most to me but  yeah I do wonder if you guys have  anything that you really want me to know  about or want to have my opinion about  then feel free to ask or tell me about  anything in the comment section and I'd  like to thank you guys for watching and  hopefully I'll see you in some planets  do video in the future not quite sure  when that's going to be but it's  definitely going to happen at some point  and I'll be playing the beta as well  anyway bye guys
 

